@node Machines
@chapter Machines

The @dfn{Machines} screen shows one card per computer on the local
network: its address on the network (for the machine raspdash runs on,
the address of its default-route interface), its operating system and
uptime, CPU usage
with a short history chart, load average, memory, swap, root file
system usage, temperatures and battery charge.  Each host is polled on
its own thread, so a host that is switched off never delays the others.
Only hosts that answer get a card: a host whose last poll failed is
left out, and the remaining cards share the whole screen, the last row
stretching across the full width.  The host comes back as soon as it
answers again.  When no host answers, the screen lists the offline
ones by name.

Every host has a @code{kind} that selects how its statistics are
collected (@pxref{Machine collectors}).  Hosts without an address, or
with @code{enabled = false}, are not shown.

